  "result": "Perfect! All 151 tests pass. I've successfully added payment tracking functionality:\n\n**Created `src/payments.js`:**\n\n**`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an invoice:\n- Validates invoice status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (error: `NOT_ISSUED`)\n- Validates amount is a positive integer (error: `AMOUNT_INVALID`)\n- Prevents overpayment beyond balance due (error: `OVERPAYMENT`)\n- Adds payment to `invoice.payments` array (creates if missing)\n- Updates status:\n  - \u2192 `'paid'` when total payments \u2265 invoice total\n  - \u2192 `'partially_paid'` when payments > 0 but < total due\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with updated invoice\n- Never mutates input invoice\n\n**`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates remaining amount owed:\n- Returns invoice total - sum of all payments\n- Handles missing payments array\n- Clamps to minimum 0 (no negative balances)\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Invoice not in issued/partially_paid status\n- `AMOUNT_INVALID` \u2014 Amount not a positive integer\n- `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 Payment exceeds balance due\n\n**Tests:** 16 new payment-specific tests covering:\n- Recording single and multiple payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Payment amount validation\n- Overpayment rejection\n- Balance calculations after payments\n- Invoice immutability\n- Integration with discounts and VAT\n\n**All 151 tests pass.** \u2705",
